摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Langfuse observability for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): exports agent sessions as OpenTelemetry trace trees (GenAI semconv) to Langfuse's OTLP endpoint","id":"gh:1333788844","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-plugin-langfuse","slug":"linyp/dsh-plugin-langfuse","topics":["agent-tracing","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","langfuse","llm-observability","opentelemetry"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Langfuse observability for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): exports agent sessions as OpenTelemetry trace tre"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"es (GenAI semconv) to Langfuse's OTLP endpoint"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-plugin-langfuse"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Langfuse observability for DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`): exports each turn as an OpenTelemetry trace — m"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"odel step → generation, tool call → tool span — groups turns by session, records session remarks and"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" message ratings as Langfuse Scores, and preserves fork/subagent lineage."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This is a community plugin (`dsh-plugin` topic), not part of the official repository. It implements "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"the harness's public telemetry seam (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-telemetry`) as an alternative backend"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" to the official OTLP-logs exporter."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"The commands below assume the installed `dsh` CLI. Running the official harness from a source checko"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ut instead? Run each of them as `pnpm dsh …` from the checkout root (after its `pnpm run build`) — s"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"ame commands, same `web` profile."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"As a profile bundle (the package ships a `cordis.patch.yml` patch layer):"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### Desktop configuration"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Config"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Field | Meaning |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### Delivery status"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## What appears in Langfuse"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| dsh session event | Langfuse concept |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| session (`session.id`) | session (`langfuse.session.id` on every exported observation/span) |\n| `t"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"urn/start` / `turn/end` | trace root observation (root span; error end reasons set span status ERROR"},{"id":"p20s3","text":") |\n| `step/start` / `step/end` + `request/header` + `request/context` + `assistant/message` | **gen"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"eration** — model, provider, safe request parameters/context window, output, canonical `gen_ai.usage"},{"id":"p20s5","text":".*` tokens (input/output/cache-read/cache-creation/reasoning); the latest assistant message also bec"},{"id":"p20s6","text":"omes the root observation's overall output. Interrupted partial output is retained and marks both ob"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"servations with `dsh.assistant.interrupted=true` without classifying the interruption as an error |\n"},{"id":"p20s8","text":"| `llm/retry` / `llm/retry-started` | structured scheduled/started events on the existing generation"},{"id":"p20s9","text":", including retry id/attempt/policy/delay and clipped failure details; no synthetic generation is cr"},{"id":"p20s10","text":"eated because the current Harness event contract provides no per-attempt usage lifecycle |\n| `assist"},{"id":"p20s11","text":"ant/message.stream` | `langfuse.observation.completion_start_time` from the first token of the commi"},{"id":"p20s12","text":"tted message, using original stream timestamps |\n| `assistant/attempt` | bounded attempt metadata on"},{"id":"p20s13","text":" the step generation; known usage is included once, with terminal outcome retained |\n| `system/messa"},{"id":"p20s14","text":"ge` / `developer/message` | event type/sequence only; system prompt text, developer content and tool"},{"id":"p20s15","text":" definitions are not exported |\n| `tool/call` + `tool/result` | tool span (arguments as input, the f"},{"id":"p20s16","text":"ull result content array as output, structured error name/code/outcome, `isError` → status ERROR; pr"},{"id":"p20s17","text":"ivate `meta` is omitted unless allowlisted) |\n| `approval/asked` + `approval/decided` | timed intern"},{"id":"p20s18","text":"al approval span under the corresponding tool when `callId` resolves, otherwise under the current ge"},{"id":"p20s19","text":"neration/turn; incomplete approvals are force-closed as ERROR |\n| `user/message` | aggregate root ob"},{"id":"p20s20","text":"servation input according to `content.turnInputMode`; deprecated trace input is retained for legacy "},{"id":"p20s21","text":"evaluator compatibility |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Architecture decisions"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### 6. What leaves the machine"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"In uploading modes, span attributes carry user and assistant message content, tool arguments and res"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ults, compaction summaries and aggregate shadow statistics, and model/usage metadata, as returned by"},{"id":"p23s3","text":" the `session-telemetry/record` waterfall. Compaction provider `rawOutput` and full `shadowedSeqs` l"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"ists are deliberately omitted. **This plugin ships no redaction rules**; a deployment exporting beyo"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"nd a trusted boundary mounts its own waterfall listener. Provider credential fields are not added by"},{"id":"p23s6","text":" this plugin; arbitrary user/tool content still requires deployment redaction. Serialized payloads a"},{"id":"p23s7","text":"re clipped at `maxAttributeChars` per attribute (default 32768); the canonical log keeps the full by"},{"id":"p23s8","text":"lipped at `maxAttributeChars` per attribute (default 32768); the canonical log keeps the full bytes."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Version compatibility"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness is in developer preview with no compatibility promises; this plugin pins exact `@de"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"epseek-ai/dsh-*` versions. Runtime DSH packages are declared as peers so Harness can reject mismatch"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"ed versions before loading the plugin; development dependencies use the same versions."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| dsh-plugin-langfuse | @deepseek-ai/dsh-* |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| 0.1.x | 0.1.0-rc.6 |\n| 0.2.x | 0.1.0-rc.6 |\n| 0.3.x | 0.1.0-rc.7 |\n| 0.4.x | 0.1.0-rc.8 |\n| 0.5.0 "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"| 0.1.0-rc.8 |\n| 0.5.1 | 0.1.1-rc.1 |\n| 0.5.2 | 0.1.2-rc.1 |\n| 0.6.0 | 0.1.5-rc.1 |\n| 0.7.0 | 0.1.7-"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"rc.1 |\n| 0.8.0 | 0.2.0-rc.2 |\n| 0.9.0 | 0.2.1-rc.2 |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The separate **Upstream compatibility canary** workflow resolves every `@deepseek-ai/*` dependency t"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"o its newest published version. Pull requests and `main` pushes are advisory; the weekly schedule an"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"d manual dispatch are strict and run source/test typechecks, unit tests, build, REAL-composition e2e"},{"id":"p28s4","text":", and package smoke. Failed runs retain the resolved manifest and lockfile for reproduction."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Known limitations and deferred work"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- **Message ratings are session-level Scores** with the original message id in metadata. They are no"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"t linked to an individual Langfuse observation; no observation id is fabricated.\n- **OTel Link UI re"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"ndering is not guaranteed**: parent/seed metadata is the stable, API-queryable lineage contract; Lan"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"gfuse may not render the Link as a clickable edge.\n- **No durable delivery** (decision 5): OTel batc"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"hing and the Score queue are in memory, so a process crash can lose accepted-but-unflushed data.\n- *"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"*One backend per context**: running Langfuse *and* the official OTLP-logs backend simultaneously req"},{"id":"p30s7","text":"uires a multi-sink evolution of the upstream seam.\n- **Auxiliary LLM calls are not generations yet**"},{"id":"p30s8","text":": title/search request events lack a complete paired completion/failure/usage lifecycle, so the plug"},{"id":"p30s9","text":"in does not fabricate observations for them.\n- **Out-of-turn generic events remain log-only**: title"},{"id":"p30s10","text":"/preset/descriptor are retained as semantic state, but the plugin does not create a long-lived sessi"},{"id":"p30s11","text":"on trace or one trace per arbitrary point event."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
